     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: DiagnosticReport space-radiation-summary-example</b></p><a name=\"space-radiation-summary-example\"> </a><a name=\"hcspace-radiation-summary-example\"> </a><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #d9e0e7; padding: 6px; margin: 4px; border: 1px solid #8da1b4; border-radius: 5px; line-height: 60%\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\"/><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Information Source: <a href=\"https://awatson1978.github.io/aerospace-medicine-ig/provenance/synthetic\">https://awatson1978.github.io/aerospace-medicine-ig/provenance/synthetic</a></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Profile: <a href=\"StructureDefinition-space-radiation-summary.html\">Space Radiation Exposure Summary</a></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px\">Tag: test health data (Details: ActReason code HTEST = 'test health data')</p></div><h2><span title=\"Codes:{https://awatson1978.github.io/aerospace-medicine-ig/CodeSystem/space-radiation-cs radiation-summary}\">Space Radiation Exposure Summary</span> (<span title=\"Codes:{http://loinc.org 73569-6}\">Radiation dose and image quality indicators</span>) </h2><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td>Subject</td><td>Jane Astronaut  Female, DoB: 1980-01-01 ( https://awatson1978.github.io/aerospace-medicine-ig/identifier/astronaut-id#AST-001)</td></tr><tr><td>When For</td><td>2025-06-01 --&gt; 2025-11-28</td></tr><tr><td>Reported</td><td>2025-12-02 09:00:00+0000</td></tr><tr><td>Performer</td><td> <a href=\"Organization-NASA.html\">Organization NASA</a></td></tr></table><p><b>Report Details</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Value</b></td><td><b>Flags</b></td><td><b>When For</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"Observation-space-radiation-exposure-example.html\"><span title=\"Codes:{https://awatson1978.github.io/aerospace-medicine-ig/CodeSystem/space-radiation-cs gcr-dose}\">Galactic Cosmic Radiation Dose</span></a></td><td>0.52 mSv<span style=\"background: LightGoldenRodYellow\"> (Details: UCUM  codemSv = 'mSv')</span></td><td>Final</td><td>2025-07-15</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"Observation-cumulative-radiation-dose-example.html\"><span title=\"Codes:{http://loinc.org 73536-5}\">Radiation dose total</span></a></td><td>94 mSv<span style=\"background: LightGoldenRodYellow\"> (Details: UCUM  codemSv = 'mSv')</span></td><td>Final</td><td/></tr></table><p>Mission dose-equivalent of 94 mSv over 180 days is consistent with the pre-flight projection of 0.5 mSv per day at solar minimum. Career total remains below the 600 mSv NASA-STD-3001 limit; no change to flight-certification status.</p></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
